Fixed both MAJOR findings in `src/lsp.rs`:

- Declared `module … end` members are recorded during the walk (honoring the last `export`) and consulted before stdlib members, including imports/aliases of declared modules.
- Alias completion now requires an in-scope `Import` binding, so aliases declared inside functions or branches no longer leak past `end`.
- Added four regression tests covering declared modules, export filtering, imported declared modules, and out-of-scope aliases.

Gates all pass: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test --all-targets` (2856 passed, 0 failed), and `verify.sh "phase-075"`.
